Implemented in [#13111](https://github.com/jdx/mise/pull/13111).

This uses an optional runtime `BackendListTools` hook rather than treating backend catalogs as static:

```lua
function PLUGIN:BackendListTools(ctx)
    return {
        tools = {
            {name = "formatter", description = "Formats source files"},
            {name = "linter", description = "Checks source files"},
        },
    }
end
```

mise prefixes those names with the installed plugin name (`plugin:formatter`), then merges them into `mise search`, shell completion, and the interactive `mise use` selector. The result is cached using the existing remote-version cache duration and timeout, invalidated when the plugin changes, and can fall back to stale data if a refresh fails. Plugins without the hook behave exactly as before, and `mise registry` remains the static registry-only command.

The hook should return a finite, useful catalog; a package-manager-style backend should not try to enumerate its entire ecosystem.

*AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: unavailable; version: unavailable.*

